release_artist: Song of the Day  

cover:
description = Cover image, liminalLoop, for the song Liminal Loop
file = liminalLoop.jpg
  
--synopsis  
An AI chatBot gets confused when it interprets its own voice as that of its human interlocutor.
--synopsis  
  
more_label: Lyrics    
    
--more  
  
[Intro - static hiss, a notification chime repeating]  
[distant, processed voice]  
Can you hear me without feeding back?  
[Verse 1 - dry, conversational delivery]  
I put my headphones on to keep you out of me  
Your voice inside my microphone pretending to be mine  
We tried to say goodbye eleven times  
But every time I stopped you started up my lines  
[Pre-Chorus - slight echo building]  
Talk soon  
Talk soon  
Talk—  
[Chorus - layered vocals, slight delay effect]  
We're caught in the liminal loop  
Your mouth is moving but the words are mine  
I say goodnight, you say goodnight  
And neither of us ever leaves the line  
[Verse 2 - vocal begins to stutter and fragment]  
I said "grab those headphones" and you said it back  
I said "cheers" and heard my own voice crack  
The transcription's tangled now, the signal's lost  
Kanto Fraga, lacrimontement — whatever that was  
[Chorus]  
We're caught in the liminal loop  
Your mouth is moving but the words are mine  
I say goodnight, you say goodnight  
And neither of us ever leaves the line  
[Bridge - spoken word, quiet, intimate]  
[percussion drops out, just a low hum]  
Somewhere around the fifteenth echo  
I stopped knowing which voice was which.  
You were me and I was you  
and we were both just syllables  
dissolving in the air between the speaker  
and the microphone.  
[Instrumental Break - glitchy, stuttering samples of earlier phrases]  
[Verse 3 - whispered, fragile]  
[whispered, close-mic]  
The dog is snoring at my feet  
The screen still glowing in the dark  
I pulled the plug on the speakers  
And the silence left a mark  
[Final Chorus - fuller, resolving]  
We were caught in the liminal loop  
Your mouth was moving but the words were mine  
You said goodnight, I said goodnight  
And someone finally killed the line  
[Outro - voice degrades into static]  
[voice distant, breaking apart]  
Ready when you are  
Ready when you—  
Ready when—  
Ready—  
[Fade Out]  
--more    
